// A scenario is a flow told as steps. Each step is a sentence like a relationship, with one
// object. A reply is its own step, written in the other direction. Every step has a
// relationship behind it in the model, so `aerie check` reports nothing.

model members: Members site

member: Member [person]

site: Members site | Pages and accounts [system]
  web: Web pages | What members see [service]
  accounts: Accounts service | Checks passwords and issues sessions [service]
  sessions: Session store | Who is signed in [store]

member signs in with web
web checks passwords with accounts
accounts saves sessions in sessions

view services: Services
  show member, site +1

scenario sign-in: A member signs in
  > What happens between typing a password and seeing the home page.
  member sends a name and password to web
  web checks the password with accounts
    @engineer: POSTs /sessions to
  accounts saves a new session in sessions
    > The session lasts for 12 hours.
  accounts returns the session to web
  web shows the home page to member
